01:05:14.550 --> 01:05:16.820
Does being a scientist
take you a lot of time?

01:05:16.820 --> 01:05:18.610
For example, sometimes
the doctor don't have

01:05:18.610 --> 01:05:19.763
much time for them.

01:05:22.970 --> 01:05:24.420
- I think so.

01:05:24.420 --> 01:05:28.310
I think the different about,
one of the different thing

01:05:28.310 --> 01:05:31.930
about being a scientist
and a doctor is yes,

01:05:31.930 --> 01:05:34.660
it takes a lot of time
training and practicing.

01:05:34.660 --> 01:05:36.900
So I think those are
both careers that require

01:05:36.900 --> 01:05:38.143
learning and practice.

01:05:39.980 --> 01:05:43.100
And, but in terms of, in terms of training

01:05:43.100 --> 01:05:48.100
that can take you for example,
four, six, or more years.

01:05:48.120 --> 01:05:49.617
So some people would do eight years.

01:05:49.617 --> 01:05:52.170
Some would do four years,
some would do three years,

01:05:52.170 --> 01:05:55.733
that's after you do your
college, four years of college.

01:05:56.700 --> 01:05:58.460
And in terms of a day-to-day,

01:05:58.460 --> 01:06:01.830
a scientist can work between, you know,

01:06:01.830 --> 01:06:06.220
three hours or 20 hours a
day, depends on the amount

01:06:06.220 --> 01:06:09.520
of work that they need to do.

01:06:09.520 --> 01:06:14.520
So I think both are, you
know, time consuming careers.

01:06:15.300 --> 01:06:17.730
But the, the difference is that I think,

01:06:17.730 --> 01:06:19.510
personally I think scientists
have more liberties

01:06:19.510 --> 01:06:22.750
of the deciding on the
day, deciding on the time,

01:06:22.750 --> 01:06:25.130
define your own schedule, especially work

01:06:25.130 --> 01:06:28.550
in a setting like this, in
a setting like universities

01:06:28.550 --> 01:06:31.177
or in nonprofit, a hospital like this.

01:06:31.177 --> 01:06:33.870
And you were more in charge of your day.

01:06:33.870 --> 01:06:34.970
You can come to work.

01:06:34.970 --> 01:06:36.600
And then for example, I have my coffee

01:06:36.600 --> 01:06:38.380
in the morning that I made at home.

01:06:38.380 --> 01:06:40.757
I come in, you know, I come in 9:30,

01:06:40.757 --> 01:06:43.390
I come in at 9:00, I come at 8:30, 10:00,

01:06:43.390 --> 01:06:46.873
but then the day takes me
to where I need it to end.

01:06:48.620 --> 01:06:50.270
I think doctors probably work more hours

01:06:50.270 --> 01:06:51.433
compared to scientists.

01:06:52.610 --> 01:06:55.320
Yeah, and then some doctors
are also scientists,

01:06:55.320 --> 01:06:58.053
so they also work in research as well.

01:06:59.390 --> 01:07:03.140
So they have both the
patient, the clinical side,

01:07:03.140 --> 01:07:04.350
and then they also work in research,

01:07:04.350 --> 01:07:05.280
they're also scientists.

01:07:05.280 --> 01:07:10.163
So yeah, it really depends
on the type of work.

01:07:12.460 --> 01:07:14.730
- [Odaelys] And one fun fact
about being a scientist,

01:07:14.730 --> 01:07:17.223
if you want to go into
school after college,

01:07:17.223 --> 01:07:20.440
and you want to go to grad
school to get a PhD degree,

01:07:20.440 --> 01:07:23.044
which takes about five to seven years,

01:07:23.044 --> 01:07:25.900
if you do it in biomedical
research or biology

01:07:25.900 --> 01:07:29.510
or one of the sciences, you
actually don't pay for school,

01:07:29.510 --> 01:07:31.940
you get paid to go to school.

01:07:31.940 --> 01:07:33.890
If you go to medical
school, it's different,

01:07:33.890 --> 01:07:35.510
you have to get paid.

01:07:35.510 --> 01:07:38.420
I think the reason why I
love being a scientist is

01:07:38.420 --> 01:07:40.100
that you also have the flexibility

01:07:40.100 --> 01:07:42.870
of doing many things after school.

01:07:42.870 --> 01:07:45.370
So you could decide to
still work in a laboratory.

01:07:45.370 --> 01:07:47.550
You can decide to work in policy.

01:07:47.550 --> 01:07:50.720
You can do consulting, you
can work with industry.

01:07:50.720 --> 01:07:54.860
So like Johnson &amp; Johnson
or Pfizer or Moderna.

01:07:54.860 --> 01:07:58.460
So there are a lot of different
options that you can do.

01:07:58.460 --> 01:08:00.960
And you come with out of school debt-free,

01:08:00.960 --> 01:08:03.110
depending on what you did for undergrad,

01:08:03.110 --> 01:08:06.710
but it's definitely a perk
with doing a PhD in science,

01:08:06.710 --> 01:08:08.593
in comparison to doing an MD.

01:08:09.690 --> 01:08:11.220
So keep that in mind if
you're thinking about

01:08:11.220 --> 01:08:13.370
going into STEM, there
are many different options

01:08:13.370 --> 01:08:16.163
outside of being a medical
doctor if you love science.

01:08:19.012 --> 01:08:22.020
- Yeah, I think both have good perks,

01:08:22.020 --> 01:08:26.484
the careers that, you
know, very involved in,

01:08:26.484 --> 01:08:31.484
in discovery and practice
and learning new things.

01:08:32.847 --> 01:08:35.516
There's also path of
MD/PhD, and you can do both.

01:08:35.516 --> 01:08:37.260
You can be a doctor and a
scientist at the same time,

01:08:37.260 --> 01:08:39.230
and that's also free.

01:08:39.230 --> 01:08:42.860
It takes between six and eight
years in addition to college.

01:08:42.860 --> 01:08:44.767
So many paths is open to you,

01:08:44.767 --> 01:08:47.450
and you don't have to get a
PhD to become a scientist.

01:08:47.450 --> 01:08:48.740
People will get a master degree,

01:08:48.740 --> 01:08:50.630
people don't have a master degree,

01:08:50.630 --> 01:08:53.560
and they decide to industry
for a couple of years first

01:08:53.560 --> 01:08:54.943
and be a scientist there.

01:08:56.490 --> 01:08:59.805
There are many, many
ways you can be involved

01:08:59.805 --> 01:09:03.330
in science and be a scientist.

01:09:03.330 --> 01:09:08.330
Yeah, so it takes time
definitely after you graduate,

01:09:09.082 --> 01:09:14.082
but yeah, it's more of like
a journey and then a career.

